      "delivery_template": "st_v1_resolver_case",
      "resolver_card_text": "Problem: Issue #316 - Add CMake Support\nContext: repo=STM32CubeH7, labels=enhancement, wontfix, projects, issue_state=closed\nResolver signal: resolution_status=candidate_fix, confidence=medium, score=0.8\nAssessment: Potential fix identified, but integration status is uncertain.\nCandidate PRs: Add CMake Support for STM32CubeH7\nCommit evidence: Added a Script to Fetch the STM32CubeH7 Package - Since this test is located in the package already, this script points to the location of the package instead of cloning the reposi | Updated README Files | Test Project Runs - Modified the test project to run on an STM32H750B-DK. | Updated README Files - Updated README files to explain the available CMake support and its usage.\nPR #317 description: # Overview\r\n\r\nThis PR adds CMake support for STM32CubeH7 as requested in issue #316.\r\n\r\nThe following changes provides CMake support to this package. Thereby allowing consuming projects to use this package as a dependency. This allows for CMake based projects to specify the necessary components and allow CMake to automatically determine which source files, header files, and include directories to make available to the consuming project.\r\n\r\n# Changes\r\n\r\n- Added CMake support\r\n  - Added `FindSTM32CubeH7.cmake` file. This file, when included via a call to `find_package()` in CMake, will automatically locate all available components in the package and create a library that the consuming project can link against.\r\n- Updated relevant README's to explain the usage of the newly available CMake support.\r\n- Added CMake tests to ensure CMake support functionality.\r\n  - Currently only uses ARM GCC to compile a test program.\nConstraints: Validate against exact MCU series, board, firmware package version, and local project config before applying.",
